## §6. Ties and Edge Cases

| Case | Specification |
|------|---------------|
| **bf16 score ties at k_eff boundary** | Stable ordering: smaller original index preferred. Deterministic across runs, even across parallel warp execution (secondary sort by index after all scores computed in Pass 1). |
| **Zero query** (‖Q[b,h,:]‖₂ < 10⁻¹²) | Clamp norm to `eps = 10⁻¹²` before division (invariant: norm ≥ eps at all times). Resulting u_Q is near-arbitrary; kernel proceeds. Do NOT raise error — zero queries occur in padding contexts. |
| **N ≤ k_eff** (sparse regime) | Set `k_eff_actual = min(k_eff, N)` inside kernel. Returns full dense attention over all N keys. Outer code may rely on this — no guard needed at the call site. |
| **N < B_block** (N < 64) | Pass 1 processes a single partial tile; heap merge handles partial array. No special case needed if tile loop uses `tile_end = min(tile_start + B_block, N)`. |
| **B=1, H=1** (unit batch/head) | Kernel must handle without implicit broadcasting. Explicitly tested in M5 validation. |
| **Empty K_cache** (N=0) | Undefined behavior for this kernel. The outer attention layer must not call the kernel when N=0. `T_dispatch=64` in DCRLlamaConfig guarantees N ≥ 64 before dispatch is enabled. |
| **Numerical overflow in exp** | The `m` subtraction (`exp(scores - m_new)`) prevents overflow in fp32 for any finite input. M1 reference must verify no NaN/inf on representative 5000-token trace. |
| **k_eff = 0** | Invalid. Caller must guarantee k_eff ≥ k_min = 64. Raise ValueError at Python boundary; not handled in Triton kernel. |
| **H not divisible by H_kv** | Invalid for Llama-3.2-1B (32 / 8 = 4 exactly). Enforce `assert H % H_kv == 0` at kernel launch. |

