## §7. Memory Layout Assumptions

### §7.1 KV cache layout (pinned to transformers 5.6.2)

HuggingFace `DynamicCache` (and `StaticCache`) at transformers 5.6.2 produces:

```
K_cache[layer_idx]: shape [B, H_kv, N, D], dtype bfloat16
    stride = (H_kv * N * D,  N * D,  D,  1)   # row-major, contiguous in N
V_cache[layer_idx]: same shape and stride
```

The N dimension is **contiguous** (stride = D in last two dims). This is required
for the sequential tile scan in Pass 1. The kernel MUST verify
`K_cache.is_contiguous()` at call time and raise if not.

If transformers upgrades to a paged or non-contiguous cache layout (e.g., PagedAttention
or newer BlockSparseCache), an adapter layer must materialize a contiguous copy before
calling the kernel. This adapter is out of scope for M2/M3; document as future work.

### §7.2 Q tensor layout

Q is the `[B, H, D]` slice from the full model attention computation, post-RoPE.
The monkey-patch layer (`dcr_attention/models/llama/attention.py`) squeezes the
sequence dimension before calling this kernel. Q is contiguous by construction.

### §7.3 Output layout

The kernel writes O as a contiguous `[B, H, D]` bf16 tensor. The caller
(monkey-patch) is responsible for inserting the sequence dimension back.

### §7.4 CUDA stream

No assumption beyond the default CUDA stream provided by `model.forward()`. The
kernel must work on the default stream without explicit synchronization.

